xpectedTile, mask=PE_MASK","B.IOT ReplacementTile, mask=PE_MASK, <last>, ->DstTile<TSize>","B.IOR BaseGPR, MinIndexGPR, MaxIndexGPR, ->zero (optional indexed range descriptor; RegSrc1=RegSrc2=zero preserves the legacy absent form)","BSTOP","When a GPR ExecutionMask is combined with a descriptor: B.IOR MaskLoGPR, MaskHiGPR, zero, ->zero, ExecMaskPresent (final record only; one/two mask words as required)"],"canonical_assembly":["MGATHER_CAS <bundle operands>"],"defaults":["B.IOR is required: RegSrc0 selects the per-PE BaseGPR; RegSrc1, RegSrc2, and RegDst must encode zero.","LB0 supplies DataTile ValidCol, LB1 supplies ValidRow, and LB2 supplies the independent physical Col; canonical macros require Col and default ValidCol to Col. Physical B.DIM omission defaults remain owned by the B.DIM contract.","IndexTile entries are S32, U32, S64, or U64 byte displacements and are not scaled or decomposed.","For indexed TLSU, RegSrc0 is the unsigned per-PE GM base. When the first B.IOR is not a legacy GPR ExecutionMask record, the selector pair (RegSrc1, RegSrc2)=(0,0) means no range descriptor; any other pair selects full-width S64 MinIndexGPR and MaxIndexGPR relative byte displacements. The one-record ExecMaskPresent form keeps its legacy Base-plus-mask meaning. A descriptor with a GPR ExecutionMask uses an unflagged Base/Min/Max first record and one final contiguous mask record with ExecMaskPresent=1."],"encoding_class":"selector-encoded-block-operation","examples":["BSTART.MGATHER.CAS DataType; B.IOT IndexTile, ExpectedTile, mask=PE_MASK; B.IOT ReplacementTile, mask=PE_MASK, <last>, ->DstTile<TSize>; B.IOR BaseGPR, zero, zero, ->zero; BSTOP","B.IOR BaseGPR, MinIndexGPR, MaxIndexGPR, ->zero (optional indexed range descriptor; RegSrc1=RegSrc2=zero preserves the legacy absent form)"],"exceptions":["Malformed bundle schema, nonzero unused B.IOR fields, unsupported datatype or layout, descriptor/shape mismatch, noncanonical predicate values, or an access fault rejects before effects."],"field_contracts":{"B.IOR.RegSrc0":{"ref":"PTO-FIELD-BLOCK-GPR-SELECTOR"}},"field_zero_meanings":{"B.IOR.RegSrc0":"The architectural zero register supplies GM base address zero."},"legality":["Only U16, U32, and U64 transfer DataTypes are accepted; packed four-bit and every other existing unsupported atomic DataType remain illegal.","Index, Expected, Replacement, and destination have equal logical valid shape and layout class.","ROWMAJOR, CUBE_M16, and CUBE_M32 are accepted; CUBE_N8 is rejected.","Participating Local Tiles share the layout class and logical coordinates while retaining independent DataType, TSize, LB2, physical columns, and capacity.","B.IOR RegSrc0 supplies BaseGPR; RegSrc1, RegSrc2, and RegDst must encode zero.","A present range descriptor supplies signed 64-bit relative byte-displacement bounds, read from the current participating PE. The current request faults with Fault_TileLegality when MinIndex > MaxIndex, before its indexed memory or Tile destination effects; committed peer effects remain. Software certifies that every participating active indexed access start byte is within the inclusive bounds and that [Base+Min, Base+Max+AccessBytes) is nonwrapping in the 64-bit GM address domain; hardware does not validate each IndexTile value against the certificate."],"memory_effects":["Each valid coordinate performs one atomic compare-and-swap at BaseGPR plus the sign- or zero-extended byte displacement.","All read/write probes complete before the first atomic effect; observed old values publish in the destination and non-valid physical elements contain PadValue."],"operands":[{"field":"destination0","role":"destination"},{"field":"address","role":"base-address"},{"field":"source0","role":"byte-displacement indices"},{"field":"source1","role":"expected"},{"field":"source2","role":"replacement"}],"ordering":["Existing PTO memory ordering and implementation-defined duplicate-address serialization are unchanged.","The optional descriptor is a conservative indexed access-set summary only. Absence or incomparable/possibly aliased translated ranges retain conservative dependence handling; interval disjointness may remove only conflict edges permitted by the existing PTO memory model and never weakens independent ordering constraints."],"standalone_opcode":false,"state_effects":["The complete physical destination region is initialized to PadValue before active valid results are published.","On success the full physical destination region is defined; a failing attempt publishes no destination."]},"contract_status":"reviewed-complete","datr_contract":{"allowed_nonzero_fields":["PadValueOrByteId","Layout"],"pad_union":"pad-value"},"depends_on":["PTO-ARCH-MEMORY-MODEL-ORDERING","PTO-BLOCK-MODEL-DISPATCH-INDEXED-TLSU-RANGE-SCHEMA","PTO-TILE-MODEL-MEMORY-ADDRESSING","PTO-TILE-MODEL-MEMORY-ATOMICS"],"disposition":"accepted-direct-operation","effect_contract":"GM_ATOM_CAS","engine":"TLSU","family":"TLSU","fault_contract":"ExecuteTileInstruction","function":8,"id":"PTO-TILE-MGATHER-CAS","legality_handler":"GM_ATOM_CAS","mnemonic":"MGATHER_CAS","name":"MGATHER_CAS","operands":[{"field":"destination0","role":"destination"},{"field":"address","role":"base-address"},{"field":"source0","role":"indices"},{"field":"source1","role":"expected"},{"field":"source2","role":"replacement"}],"restart_contract":"CompleteBundleAtWithAcceptedApplicabilityRules","semantic_handler":"GM_ATOM_CAS","state_effects":["operand:destination0:destination","operand:address:base-address","operand:source0:indices","operand:source1:expected","operand:source2:replacement"],"summary":"atomic compare-and-swap gather using explicit byte displacements.","surface":"tile"}

